-- title:
--   Differentials of a local algebra with retraction are multiples of dt
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings with $S$ an $R$-algebra, let $S$ be local, and assume the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{S/R}$ is finite (finitely generated) as an $S$-module. Let $\pi \colon S \to R$ be a homomorphism of $R$-algebras — so in particular $\pi$ is a retraction of the structure map $R \to S$ — and write $I = \ker \pi$ for the kernel of the underlying ring homomorphism. Let $t \in S$ satisfy $\pi(t) = 0$, and assume the inclusion of ideals $I \subseteq (t) + I^2$, where $(t)$ is the ideal generated by $t$. Then for every $\omega \in \Omega_{S/R}$ there exists $g \in S$ with $\omega = g \cdot \mathrm{d}t$, where $\mathrm{d} =$ `KaehlerDifferential.D R S` is the universal $R$-derivation of $S$. Equivalently, $\Omega_{S/R}$ is generated over $S$ by the single element $\mathrm{d}t$; the statement is given in the pointwise existential form, with no claim that $g$ is unique.
--
--   This is the standard consequence of the conormal sequence for a section $\pi$ of $S/R$: if $\ker\pi$ is generated modulo its square by $t$, then $\Omega_{S/R}$ is a cyclic $S$-module on $\mathrm{d}t$, i.e. $t$ serves as a local parameter for differentials. It is used in the analysis of differentials on rational curve models of modular curves near a cusp, where it produces a generator of the module of differentials against which $q$-expansions are compared.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_KaehlerDifferential_exists_eq_smul_D_of_retraction_of_ker_le_span_sup_sq.lean

